.KEY HOST,PORT/N
.BRA {
.KET }
; ClaudeCode: Claude Code on the NAS (your Claude subscription), in this
; window. The NAS asks for the uptelnet password (set on the NAS with
; setpw; it is never stored here), then Claude Code starts in tmux --
; quit it or lose the line and the session is still there next time.
;   ClaudeCode                      the host and port in ENVARC:Claude/remote
;                                   (the file `Claude SETUP` writes; the port is
;                                   2323 when the line has none)
;   ClaudeCode HOST [PORT]          that NAS address; the port is 2323 when left out
; From Workbench: double-click its icon (IconX opens an UP-Term window).
If "{HOST}" EQ ""
  If NOT EXISTS ENVARC:Claude/remote
    Echo "ClaudeCode: no address given and ENVARC:Claude/remote does not exist."
    Echo "Run `Claude SETUP` once to store the address, or start with: ClaudeCode HOST [PORT]"
    Quit 10
  EndIf
  ; the first line that is not a ';' comment and has a port (Search prints it
  ; into ENV:ClaudeCodeRemote, which $ClaudeCodeRemote expands to), else the
  ; first one with only a host
  Search >ENV:ClaudeCodeRemote ENVARC:Claude/remote "[~;]#? #[0-9]#?" PATTERN NONUM
  If NOT WARN
    uptelnet $ClaudeCodeRemote
    Delete >NIL: ENV:ClaudeCodeRemote QUIET
    Quit 0
  EndIf
  Search >ENV:ClaudeCodeRemote ENVARC:Claude/remote "[~; ]#?" PATTERN NONUM
  If NOT WARN
    uptelnet $ClaudeCodeRemote 2323
    Delete >NIL: ENV:ClaudeCodeRemote QUIET
    Quit 0
  EndIf
  Delete >NIL: ENV:ClaudeCodeRemote QUIET
  Echo "ClaudeCode: ENVARC:Claude/remote names no host. Run `Claude SETUP`,"
  Echo "or start with: ClaudeCode HOST [PORT]"
  Quit 10
EndIf
uptelnet {HOST} {PORT$2323}
